          "date": "2026-11-17 10:39:27.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-18317 libcfs: parse IPv6 o2ib NIDs in userspace",
        "message": "LU-18317 libcfs: parse IPv6 o2ib NIDs in userspace\n\nThe kernel gained support for IPv6 addresses on o2ib NIDs in commit\n22667e91b1 (\"LU-18317 lnet: fix configure o2ib NID with IPv6\naddress\") by adding the size-aware nf_addr2str_size and\nnf_str2addr_size parsers to the O2IBLND netstrfns entry.  The\nuserspace copy of the same table was not updated, so mount.lustre\nstill rejects an IPv6 o2ib NID that the kernel accepts:\n\n  mount.lustre: Unsupported NID '6699:7654::1234:1234:d84@o2ib'\n  mount.lustre: Can't parse NID '6699:7654::1234:1234:d84@o2ib'\n\nlibcfs_strnid() falls back to the 32-bit nf_str2addr (IPv4 only) when\nnf_str2addr_size is absent, which is why tcp parses IPv6 NIDs but o2ib\ndoes not.  Add the same two fields to the userspace O2IBLND entry so\nmount.lustre parses IPv6@o2ib NIDs like the kernel does.\n\nAssisted-by: Augment Agent:DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\nSigned-off-by: Lai Siyao <lai.siyao@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: Ia68b13787062b1e7e0c91ce3152892744692781b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
